  (iii) **Runtime census by tripwire.** In a scratch copy of the harness's database creation (read `apps/api/test/harness.ts` to find where the schema is created; a scratch copy in your `-mut` tree only, never committed), install `BEFORE UPDATE OF policy_target_key OR INSERT ON pc.policy` triggers that, when `OLD.policy_target_key IS NOT NULL` and the statement sets the column (changed OR equal), write one row to a scratch table (txid, old, new, `current_query()`) **and let the statement proceed** (the log row must survive: log through `dblink`/an autonomous side channel only if available, else RAISE with a distinctive SQLSTATE the test run reports, and say which you used). Run the **whole API db group** at main (+ the new file copied in: expect the tripwire to fire for the new file's R1/R2/same-key rows, which is the positive control) and at the head (expect 0 fires): print the fire list by test file and row. A fire at the head from any file = Blocker of the class (G-1). Control: with the helper call deleted from `completeExpertSetup` (your `-mut` swap) the new file's rows fire the tripwire. If the harness cannot host the trigger, say so, mark this frame NOT TESTED, and the verdict is conditional.
  (iv) **Black-box sweep of every mutating operation of the contract.** List the served contract's mutating operations (`POST|PUT|PATCH|DELETE` operation ids from the committed `packages/api-contract/src/openapi.json`, counted, control: a planted id is found; do not read a hosted document). On each of three states (a pending Guided start holding a planted target R2; the same planted R1; a completed start holding a target set by `setPolicyTarget`) and for every role the operation allows, send a minimal valid request (and, for each operation that accepts a policy target key in its body, one carrying a DIFFERENT key and one carrying the SAME key: expected at least `createEngagement`, `createGuidedEngagement`, `cloneEngagement`, `completeExpertSetup`, `setPolicyTarget`, `createSetupDraft`/`updateSetupDraft`, `updateEngagement`, `createDraft`; derive the list from the contract, do not take it from here). After each, read `policy_target_key` of the policy by the superuser client: unchanged for the source policy in every case; a clone or a create makes a NEW policy (different `policy_id`), and that new policy holding a key is not a second target (print the ids). Frame: the number of operations, states, roles, requests sent; a response that is 5xx = a finding of its own. Control: at main the `completeExpertSetup` cell with a different key on R1 and R2 DOES move the key (the defect, reproduced by you with your own request before any head run).
  (v) **The refusal writes nothing.** For `completeExpertSetup` carrying a key on R1, R2, and a completed-start-with-target (the last is refused earlier by `EXPERT_SETUP_NOT_PENDING`: say which refusal fires), with the key DIFFERENT and the SAME, and with each earlier refusal present at once (stale pin, stale If-Match, no If-Match, blank environment, repeated approvers, unlinked approver, unknown key): your **state dumper** digest before and after is equal (every `pc.*` table of the tenant, the audit and idempotency tables included), the engagement and version ETags are equal, and the placeholder approver is still there. Control: the same request at main (defect) changes the digest; a request that succeeds changes it. **Read how the transaction wrapper (`inEngagement`/`operation`) rolls back on a throw and whether any audit, idempotency or outbox row is written in a SECOND transaction on a refusal** (static, and the digest shows it at runtime). The builder says position inside the transaction is unobservable by row-equality (a throw rolls back); the tripwire row proves "no write is tried first": **re-derive it with YOUR tripwire on every table `completeExpertSetup` writes (approver INSERT, approver DELETE, engagement UPDATE, policy UPDATE, framework_selection, version bump, audit): at the head none is attempted before the refusal; control: swap the check to after the approver loop and the tripwire fires.**
- **C3. The sentence is the same bytes; no new word; nothing else about the answer changed.** FAIL: `detail` of the new 409 not byte-equal to (a) `setPolicyTarget`'s answer for a completed start holding a target at the head, (b) the same call at main, (c) the string literal in the source at main (`git show`), as three `sha256`s of the `detail` bytes (control: a one-character edit in a scratch copy of the literal changes the hash and the program reports it); the problem body's other members (`type`/`code`/`title`/`status`/`instance` shape, headers incl. `content-type`) not equal to `setPolicyTarget`'s apart from the operation's own path/instance (print the two key sets). **NEW WORDS (your program, not the builder's `diffcheck.py`):** over `git diff -U0 0b52848c c2f0b789 -- apps/api/src/routes/engagements.ts`, every string literal and template literal in added lines versus removed lines; the multiset of words of the added literals minus the removed must be empty (control: a planted extra word prints a non-empty set); no new `code`, no new HTTP status in any `conflict(`/`problem(` call; `packages/api-contract/**` blobs equal (C1). The contract's notes for `completeExpertSetup` do not mention the new refusal (the builder left them; a **Note**, with the line, as a decision for Tuesday; the status 409 is already declared for the operation: print the `problems` list of the operation in `document.ts`). **The web surface (static, read-only):** how `apps/web/src/screens/w1/problems.ts:39` and `EngagementDetails.tsx:362` handle `POLICY_TARGET_ALREADY_CHOSEN`, and whether the set-up card's submit handler maps a 409 of this code to the server `detail` or to a generic failure (print the lines; a hole = Note, the card's behaviour in a browser is NOT TESTED).
- **C4. Everything else answers as before (the differential).** FAIL: any cell of the battery that differs between main's tree and the head's tree, other than the new refusal cell(s). **Battery (yours; frame printed):** states {pending Guided start without a target; pending with R1; pending with R2; completed Guided start with a target; completed without; an Expert-created (non-Guided) engagement} x operations {`completeExpertSetup` with: no key; a key; a key plus a name; each earlier refusal alone and together with a key (stale pin, stale If-Match, none, blank environment, repeated approvers, unlinked approver, unknown key); `setPolicyTarget` on each state with same/different/unknown key, stale pin, stale ETag; `getEngagement`; `updateEngagement`} (count the cells; expected >= 60). Expected differing cells: exactly those of {pending with R1, pending with R2} x {`completeExpertSetup` with a valid key}, which turn 200 into 409. **The first-target path:** on a pending start WITHOUT a target, `completeExpertSetup` with a key is 200, `policy.policy_target.key` equals the key, the draft's Essential Eight selection is the target's (edition, level), the placeholder approver is replaced, the audit action is `engagement.expert_setup_completed` carrying `policy_target_key`; the same bytes at main and at the head. **Setups without a key:** on a planted start (R1, R2) and on an unplanted start, no key = 200 at main and head, target and level unchanged, approvers replaced. **Precedence table:** for a planted start, each earlier refusal combined with a valid key answers its own code (the new 409 comes after them all) at the head exactly as at main's order of refusals (print the table).
- **C5. Concurrency: two concurrent completes on one policy.** FAIL: both complete (two 200s), or the policy ends with a target other than the winner's, or the winner's approvers/selection differ from the target, or a deadlock (`40P01`) or 5xx. **Race harness (yours; deterministic, not luck):** hold the engagement row with a superuser transaction (`SELECT ... FOR UPDATE`), fire both requests, wait until `pg_stat_activity` shows both sessions waiting on a lock (print the count; timeout 20 s: a harness that cannot hold both is DEAD, say so), release, collect. **Scenarios, N repetitions each (N >= 20; print N and each outcome tally):** (a) two completes with DIFFERENT keys on a pending start with no target: expected exactly one 200 and the other 409 (`EXPERT_SETUP_NOT_PENDING` if the engagement lock serialises them, or `POLICY_TARGET_ALREADY_CHOSEN`: print which, per repetition); final target = the winner's key, one selection, one placeholder-free approver set; (b) two completes with the SAME key; (c) two completes, one with a key and one without; (d) a complete with a key vs `setPolicyTarget` (the latter must be `EXPERT_SETUP_PENDING` or `POLICY_TARGET_ALREADY_CHOSEN`, never a second write); (e) two completes with keys on a PLANTED start: both 409, nothing written; (f) lock-order probe: run (a) and (d) with the lock-wait graph logged (`pg_locks`/`pg_stat_activity` sample) and say whether `completeExpertSetup` (engagement row, then version, then policy) and `setPolicyTarget` (version, then policy) can form a cycle (static reading of both orders AND the runtime tally of `40P01`). **The `FOR UPDATE` in the helper:** swap it out (your `-mut` file) and re-run (a)-(e): if every outcome is unchanged because the engagement lock already serialises completes, say so (the lock is redundant for the set-up path and is exercised only by `setPolicyTarget`; a **Note** with the tally); if an outcome changes, that is a finding. The builder has NO concurrency row: the absence is a **Note** (or a **Minor** if you show a reachable interleaving the new rows would not catch) with your harness's result attached as ticket text.
- **C6. The rows and the swaps (the red-proofs, yours), the suites, names.** In `wt-b724-mut` (never committed; plain text swaps you write, anchor count 1 each, one mutant file per swap, each restore `cmp`-equal to the head file; a mutant that does not load or typecheck is reported as that, never as a kill; a failing assertion is quoted from the TEXT reporter):
  (a) **Rows red at base by name:** the head's new test file run against main's `engagements.ts` (a tree `wt-b724-main` + the new file): the builder's red set is R2, R1, same key, order, tripwire (5 of 9); print yours by title, with the failing assertion, and show the other 4 green (the keyless-complete row, the no-target control, and the two `setPolicyTarget` controls). A row red for a reason other than "the call answered 200 and moved the key" (a harness error, a plant refused by the database, a wrong ETag) is not evidence = Major of the class (G-3).
  (b) **Your own swaps, each turning its named row(s) red and the rest green:** S1 the helper call in `completeExpertSetup` deleted; S2 the call moved after the approver INSERT loop; S3 the call moved after `recordPolicyTarget`; S4 the condition `target !== null` dropped (check also without a key); S5 the helper's null test turned into "refuse only when the held key differs from the requested one" (the same-key row must go red); S6 the helper's null test turned into `rows.length > 0` (a control row goes red or not: report); S7 `setPolicyTarget`'s call replaced by its old inline text (a behaviour-neutral refactor: every row green; this proves the lift changed nothing); S8 the sentence changed by one character in the helper (the byte-equal rows and `b144`/`b113` rows red by name); S9 the check placed before `refuseStalePin`/`lockDraft` (the order row red); S10 `FOR UPDATE` dropped from the helper (C5's tally decides). **Every swap that stays green under all 9 rows and the neighbour files = the row set cannot fail there: name it** (S2/S3 are expected to be red only through the tripwire row; a position the throw-and-rollback makes unobservable is a **Note**, not a Major, when your tripwire proves the property holds: say which). Controls: unmutated 0 red (ran 9), a trailing comment added 0 red, a whitespace-equivalent change 0 red.
  (c) **Tests and suites (Composer heavy rules).** CI predicates: Composer has no test workflow; `scripts/ci.sh` runs every step, a step PASS only on exit 0 (the node step `node: lint, format, typecheck, build, test (--network none)`; the db step `scripts/test-db.sh` runs `npx vitest run --config packages/db/vitest.config.ts && npx vitest run --config apps/api/vitest.db.config.ts` in a network-less container against the digest-pinned `postgres:16`, inspect locally, never pull; re-read the lines and write the pass predicate in STATUS). At the head tree in `pc-b724-node:head`: the new file alone **9 of 9, rc 0, 3 consecutive runs**; each row alone once by `-t` (9 of 9); the **whole API db group** (`apps/api/vitest.db.config.ts`) at the head and at main `8347f91b` through `dbone.sh`'s postgres route: **head = main + 1 file and + 9 tests, failures 0** (your own baseline, printed; the builder's 80/1492 and 81/1501 are on an older base); the **unit chain** (`unit.sh ci`: whole-repo `npm run lint`, `npm run format:check`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm run build`, then `vitest run`, the contract file `packages/api-contract/src/openapi.test.ts` included) rc 0 each on the head and on main (a rc non-zero only on the head = Major); `prettier --check` and `eslint` on the two paths alone; `tsc` of the new test file by a scratch tsconfig under `.tools/b724` (control: `--listFilesOnly` lists it, a planted type error gives rc 2). The `packages/db` group is NOT re-run (no `packages/db` byte; say so under NOT TESTED). **Names** (your own tokenizer over the static `it(`/`test(`/`describe(` titles and the runner's JSON reporter, main vs head): lost 0, added 9 (control: one title dropped lost 1), no duplicate title. A red only under load and green re-run alone at load1 below 6 is a load artefact: record both.
- **C7. CodeQL, checks, merge, overlap, claims, secrets.** FAIL: any check-run on the head not `completed` `success`/`neutral` at the verdict; an open alert on the PR ref, the merge ref or main; an analysis of the head missing; a merge ref whose parents are not main and the head. `check-runs --paginate` at start, mid and verdict with the time (expected `CodeQL`, `Analyze (csharp)`, `Analyze (javascript-typescript)`, all `completed` `success` at the drafter's 09:54 read; **if any run is `in_progress` or `queued` at a read, poll every 60 s and WAIT for every run to complete, at most 40 minutes beyond your last heavy job; never conclude from a partial set**); `code-scanning/analyses?ref=refs/pull/95/head` (`commit_sha`, `results_count`, `error`; control `ref=refs/heads/main` returns rows); alerts in ALL states on `refs/pull/95/head`, `refs/pull/95/merge`, main (dismissed equal at start and verdict; you never dismiss). The added source lines are one parameterised `SELECT ... WHERE policy_id = $1` and a `throw`; no input-built query, `RegExp`, file path or log (print the method; the new test file builds SQL from fixed strings and bound parameters: read every `query(` call in it, count the ones with a template literal, control a planted `new RegExp(` line is flagged). **Merge in YOUR plain clone:** `git clone --no-hardlinks '<project>/2_Project_Files' '<project>/.tools/b724/repo'` (never `--shared`; push URL `DISABLED-no-push`; prove the shared `.git/objects` mtime and `for-each-ref` count unchanged), ONE explicit fetch `'+refs/heads/main:refs/remotes/origin/main' '+refs/pull/95/head:refs/remotes/origin/pr95'` (no `--prune`; retry a `Permission denied (publickey)` 5x): **re-read main with `ls-remote` first (it was `8347f91b` at the draft) and say if it moved**; `rev-list --left-right --count origin/main...origin/pr95` = `1 1` while main is `8347f91b`; `git merge-tree --write-tree origin/main origin/pr95` rc 0 and its tree compared with the merge ref's tree `eef94aba633cc5485609d00b9422d8605f84c59d` (equal while main is unmoved); the merge result's diff against main = the two paths = `pulls/95/files`; control: a scratch branch changing the SAME lines of `engagements.ts` differently conflicts (rc 1). `pulls/95` `mergeable` / `mergeable_state` and `refs/pull/95/merge` parents + tree at start and verdict (check parents on every read: the ref lags a push by minutes). **Overlap by GET:** `pulls/<n>/files --paginate` for #94, #91, #86, #85 (and any PR opened since) against the two paths by `/usr/bin/grep -c -x -F` (controls: self-compare of #95 lists 2, a planted shared path found), plus every live `b6*`/`b7*` branch by `compare` (squash-merged history branches are listed, not stops). **Claims (the builder STATUS, line by line):** a `PRIOR WORK` section exists (heading found by `/usr/bin/grep -n -i`), the 9 rows, the 5-of-9 red at base, M1-M4, "nothing written", "NEW WORDS added 0", "sentence literal count 1 before and after", the unit numbers (re-run at your own base), "No process of mine", the one `rm -f` disclosure (a builder rule breach of its own commission: a **Note**; no product byte), "the author field": a **Note**, no name quoted. A claim your run contradicts = Major if it hides a defect, Minor if only a number. gitleaks `/opt/homebrew/bin/gitleaks`: a RANDOM `ghp_`-shaped canary written at run time into a scratch directory rc 1 FIRST (typed into no file of the project), then `0b52848c..c2f0b789` AND `8347f91b..c2f0b789` rc 0, chained with `&&` in `bash -c`. Evidence and `.tools/b724/` hold 0 non-ASCII bytes (`LC_ALL=C /usr/bin/grep -c '[^ -~]'`, control: a planted byte counts 1), no person's name, no card slug, no four-underscore run. At the end: nothing of yours running, lock released by move into `quarantine/locks/`, containers, networks, images and trees named with state, every scratch change restored byte-equal (sha256), refs before/after in your clone (added only `refs/remotes/origin/*`, removed 0), no ref on origin, no PR comment, no push, `lsof -nP -iTCP:9990-9999 -sTCP:LISTEN` rc 1.
Priority if short: C2 and C6(a)-(b) first (the heart), C1 (cheap, first in time), C5, C4, C3, C6(c), C7. A verdict from a gate that did not finish C2, C5, C6(a)-(b) and the new file's runs at the head is conditional and never a clean GO.

## GRADING (binding; the ONE table; capability decides)
- **G-1 delta, routes and no-loosening (C1, C2).** A path beyond the two, or a byte of the contract, `apps/web`, `packages/db`, `DEPLOY.md`, a package/config/lock file, or an existing test = **Blocker**; **any route, operation, function or trigger that delivers a second target to a policy that holds one = Blocker, class**; a refusal that leaves any row written (state digest differs) = **Blocker, class**; a second commit or a moved head = STOP; a person's name, real customer name, secret or decision-card slug in an added line or message = **Blocker**; an assertion removed or loosened or any removed line of `engagements.ts` beyond the inlined check = **Major, class**; a ticket key in the PR title, or a work number in an added title or comment where the file has none = **Minor**.
- **G-2 the answer (C3, C4).** A new word-bearing literal, new code or status, or a contract byte = **Major** (and a STOP: a new sentence is the product owner's); `detail` not byte-equal to `setPolicyTarget`'s = **Major, class**; any differential cell other than the new refusal = **Major, class** (a changed answer on a path the brief lists as unchanged); the first-target path or a keyless set-up broken = **Blocker**; the contract notes not mentioning the refusal, the web card's handling unproved = **Note**.
- **G-3 closure and the rows (C6a-b).** A named row red under no revert or swap = **Major, class**; a row red at base for a wrong reason = **Major, class**; a swap that stays green under every row and is observable by the tripwire or a differential cell = **Major, class**; a swap unobservable by any instrument (a position within one rolled-back transaction) = **Note**; a revert that turns more or fewer rows red than the builder claimed = **Minor** (name them) unless a named row is lost, then Major; the builder's claim your run contradicts = **Major** if it hides a defect, **Minor** if only a number.
- **G-4 concurrency (C5).** Two 200s, a policy ending with a target other than the winner's, a deadlock, or a 5xx under a race = **Blocker, class**; the helper lock redundant on the set-up path, or no concurrency row = **Note** (ticket text with your harness attached); a reachable interleaving the rows would not catch = **Minor**.
- **G-5 stability, CI, CodeQL (C6c, C7).** A whole-suite red you reproduce twice = **Major**; the new file other than 9 of 9, or the head's group other than main + 1 file + 9 tests, without a reason = a finding at the severity of its cause; names lost or added other than 0 / 9 = **Major**; lint/format/typecheck non-zero on the head and zero on main = **Major**; a load-only red = artefact (record both runs); a failing check-run on the head or merge result = **Major**; `in_progress` at the verdict = `CI pending: <names>`, at most GO WITH FOLLOW-UPS; an analysis of the head missing = NOT scanned; an open alert on the head or merge ref = **Blocker** and a STOP; a textual conflict = **Major**; a path shared with #94, #91, #86, #85 or another live lane = **Major**; a merge ref still on other parents after 10 minutes of polling = a Note (recompute in your clone) and `CI pending: merge ref`; a missing PRIOR WORK = returned. **Always Note:** the author field, dependabot's vulnerabilities line, the squash artefact (the PR title becomes the squash subject).
- **G-6 the verdict follows the table, and the cap.** Any Blocker, or any Major of the class = `NO GO round 1 of 2`: FOR TUESDAY then carries the CLOSED list (with cells), the RESIDUE as ticket text with the tester's cells attached, and the fix shape in prose (one new commit on the same branch). Notes and Minors only = `GO` or `GO WITH FOLLOW-UPS` (list the Deferred rows and any Minor; decisions in FOR TUESDAY). Add ` (conditional: <reason>)` for any required check not run; `CI pending` is always conditional.

## LOAD (binding; Composer docker route)
8 cores shared with other projects' seats (load1 read 6-10 at the draft; a Composer builder may start beside you). Heavy = `docker build`, any database-test container, the unit chain, any vitest over more than one file, the race and battery runs against postgres. **Start a heavy job only while `uptime` load1 is below 7 at two reads 4 s apart** (not independent reads: say so), recorded beside the result; at or over, poll every 20 s, log each wait, do light work meanwhile (C1, the static census, the clone, the harness code, the C7 polls). **One heavy job of yours at a time**, behind `<project>/.tools/b724/lock` (copied `heavy.sh`; released by MOVE to `.tools/b724/quarantine/locks/`, never `rmdir`) and the cross-seat `ps` gate. A MOVING heartbeat (counter plus `date`) to `.tools/b724/logs/heartbeat.txt` every 30 s from every waiter and long job. A wait loop never uses `pgrep -f` on a pattern in its own command line (wait on a recorded PID, `wait $!`, or a done-marker file). Every command gets its input or none (`/dev/null`). NO artificial load. Build `pc-b724-node:head` once from the head's tree: `docker build --pull=false --progress=plain -f <tree>/docker/Dockerfile --target ci -t pc-b724-node:head <tree>` (an ABSOLUTE `-f`); record node, npm, vitest, tsc versions (RELAYED by the builder: v22.23.2, 10.9.8). One image serves main and the head only if the lockfile blobs are equal (they are: no package byte moved; prove it by `rev-parse` of both); the unit chain needs the image built from the tree it judges, so build `pc-b724-node:main` too only if `npm ci` of the second differs (it will be a cache hit; say so). The mutant sweeps run through `dbone.sh` mounts of `-mut`. Plan the container starts (new file 3x, 9 rows alone, group at main and head, two unit runs, the differential and race harness, up to 10 swaps in 2-3 batches) and write the budget at Step 0 (about 40). Remove ONLY your own `pc-b724-*` containers, networks and anonymous postgres volumes, by exact name.

## HOLDS
Datasec / Security Composer only; if any output shows another client's material, stop and disclose its shape. No deploy, `az`, Kudu, Entra, Graph, ssh. **No HTTP to any hosted or production host or the demo site** (the app under test runs in-process or in your own container with no published port). Never `docker exec`/`stop`/`rm`/`logs` against a container you did not create (the copied `dbtest.sh` execs into the database container it created itself). Network: your one in-clone `git fetch`, `gh api -X GET` under the project `GH_CONFIG_DIR`, nothing else; `gh run rerun`, `gh workflow run` and any POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE are forbidden; never dismiss an alert. Git in the project repo `2_Project_Files`: READ verbs only (`--no-optional-locks`: ls-remote, log, show, diff, cat-file, ls-tree, rev-parse, rev-list, merge-base, grep, config --get); clone, fetch, worktree add, merge-tree only inside `.tools/b724/repo` and `.tools/wt-b724-*`. **HP-NDA hold:** never open `HP Reporting and Docs/`, any SOW, `1_Project_Definition/Source_Documents/` contents or `inbound/` folders. **The unit step's Essential Eight SOW text input is passed ONLY as a read-only bind mount into a `--network none` container, at the path the copied `unit.sh` already names (`PC_E8_SOW_TEXT`); stat it with `[ -f ]`; never open, print, grep, hash or quote it.** The Stamp slot "Stamped by" records Tuesday's `Q-2` answer; no answer reads NO, the bind mount is not made, and the unit rows that need the SOW text are NOT TESTED (the other unit steps still run). No decision-queue tool, scoreboard, Artifact, Docs, mail, chat or publish tool. Secrets only as environment; never open `4_Credentials/.env` except the NAME test, never `3_Access_Keys/`. **Never delete** (`rm`, `branch -D`, `reset`, `clean`, `stash`, `prune`): quarantine to `.tools/b724/quarantine/`. **Never `cd`**; absolute single-quoted paths (they hold a space and `!`); write `${VAR}:path`; no unquoted word starting with `=`; no unquoted `$VAR` holding a command with spaces; multi-step chains under `bash -c` or a quoted-heredoc script; `/usr/bin/grep -i` with a positive control for every count; `python3 -I` for anything reading a file you did not write; read your scripts back and scan for non-ASCII. Scratch changes (planted rows, triggers, swaps) live ONLY in `wt-b724-mut`, `wt-b724-probe`, `.tools/b724/scratch/` and the throwaway test database; never in a committed file, never against a database that is not the throwaway container's. No person's name in any id, file or STATUS (say "the product owner"; do not quote git author fields), no card slug, clock from `date`. Nothing to any human. **STANDING LINES:** PRIOR-WORK CHECK (your STATUS carries a PRIOR WORK section naming what you read of the builder lane and the earlier gates and what you reuse; a READY-class verdict without one is returned); no message to any human; Jira writes none; never delete (quarantine). **RESUME at about 80% of context or at the hard stop:** write `PROGRESS` and `RESUME` sections (each check done/partial/not started with evidence paths; next commands; every scratch tree with its restore proof; lock released), stop your processes and containers, end `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY` with the one question "continue in a fresh seat from RESUME?". **Usage pause:** if your session ends at the account's weekly limit, that is the platform, not a STOP; on resume re-read your own STATUS last line, re-pin main, the head and the checks, release or reclaim any lock you held by your own rule, and carry on against the hard stop Tuesday names in an addendum.

